CM 1MHz_tower, trimmed to the cards the symmetric cell acts on (momwire#415).
CM Source: xnec2c examples/1MHz_tower.nec, a top-loaded 1 MHz tower whose
CM four legs each carry an 85 uH inductor to ground and which is fed at one
CM of them.  GR 3 4 rotates the leg-and-loading assembly (tags 1, 2, 3) into
CM four, so the cell is 25 wires / 42 segments of 100 / 168 and the copies
CM carry tags 4-6, 7-9 and 10-12.  The one LD here addresses tag 3, INSIDE
CM the cell, so the inductor lands on all four legs.
CM The corpus deck writes four LD cards -- tags 3, 6, 9 and 12, one per leg.
CM Under NEC's own rule the last three are silently dropped and the first is
CM replicated onto them, so the physics is this deck's; momwire refuses that
CM form rather than following NEC into silence.  See 1MHz_tower_dropped.deck.
CM One frequency inside the corpus deck's own sweep; NE/NH/RP trimmed away.
